# Build context for the release image (Dockerfile at the repository root).
# Allowlist: everything is excluded except what `cargo build --release` needs,
# so target/, .git/ and local scenes and images never reach the builder.
# Add new crate sources here (build.rs, workspace members, ...).
#
# The dev container (.devcontainer/Dockerfile) shares this file: its features
# make the devcontainer CLI build a generated copy of that Dockerfile from
# /tmp, so a Dockerfile.dockerignore beside it is never read. It needs
# rust-toolchain.toml and scripts/install-tools.sh.
#
# .cargo/ stays out on purpose: its config.toml sets target-cpu=native, which
# would tie the image to the CI runner's CPU. The Dockerfile sets RUSTFLAGS.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!rust-toolchain.toml
!crates/
!scripts/install-tools.sh
